{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Take your station by your burnt offering.</b> To direct intention with the offering up of each part of it, according to the principle that כִּי הַדָּם הוּא בַּנֶּפֶשׁ יְכַפֵּר (Leviticus 17:11)." "<b>Perhaps YHWH will chance to meet me.</b> Perhaps in my isolation — even though I cannot attain ascent to the light of the King's presence as was the case with Moses, of whom it says וּבְכָל בֵּיתִי נֶאֱמָן הוּא (Numbers 12:7) — it may chance to me that YHWH will come to meet me, as was the case with Moses at the beginning of his prophecy, before he ascended to the perfection he attained afterward, as it says: וַיַּרְא ה׳ כִּי סָר לִרְאוֹת וַיִּקְרָא אֵלָיו אֱלֹהִים (Exodus 3:4)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:53.767021331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}